ge\n3. **Storage**: Encrypted data requires slightly more space\n4. **Memory**: Secure operations may use more RAM\n\n### Security Maintenance\n1. **Regular Updates**: Keep security libraries updated\n2. **Vulnerability Scanning**: Regular security assessments\n3. **Certificate Management**: Monitor certificate expiration\n4. **Compliance**: Ensure regulatory compliance\n\n## Next Steps\n\n### Immediate Actions Required\n1. **Configure Email Credentials**: Set up proper email authentication\n2. **Test Security Features**: Validate all security implementations\n3. **Update Calling Code**: Modify existing code to use SecurityManager\n4. **Monitor Performance**: Check for any performance impacts\n\n### Future Enhancements\n1. **Certificate Pinning**: Implement for all external services\n2. **Biometric Authentication**: Add user authentication for sensitive operations\n3. **Security Analytics**: Add security event logging and monitoring\n4. **Compliance**: Implement additional compliance requirements (GDPR, etc.)\n\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] SecurityManager initialization\n- [ ] Credential storage and retrieval\n- [ ] Signature encryption/decryption\n- [ ] Dropbox client creation with secure credentials\n- [ ] Email sending with secure credentials\n- [ ] Network security enforcement\n- [ ] File access restrictions\n- [ ] Legacy device compatibility\n- [ ] Performance impact assessment\n- [ ] Security status monitoring\n\n## Support\n\nFor questions about the security implementation:\n1. Review the SecurityManager class documentation\n2. Check security status using diagnostic methods\n3. Verify network security configuration\n4. Test email configuration before deployment\n5. Monitor logs for security-related messages\n\n---\n\n**Security Level**: Enterprise-grade with hardware-backed protection\n**Compliance**: Suitable for handling sensitive delivery and customer data\n**Maintenance**: Requires periodic security updates and credential rotation"}"}}]},{"role":"tool",